    "body": "### Problem\n\n`:restart` (and loading a session while the buffer is already open) fails with E95 for named `buftype=acwrite` buffers, as used by plugins with `BufReadCmd` / `BufWriteCmd` such as oil.nvim (`oil://`) and kube.nvim (`kube://`):\n\n```\nError in UIEnter Autocommands for \"*\":\nE5108: Lua: ...restart_session_Q2mEZU, line 25: Vim(file):E95: Buffer with this name already exists\n```\n\n`:mksession` writes such a buffer as\n\n```vim\nbadd +0 foo://bar\n...\nenew\nfile foo://bar\n```\n\nbecause `put_view()` (src/nvim/ex_session.c) only uses `:edit` when `!bt_nofilename(buf)`, and Nvim's `bt_nofilename()` (src/nvim/buffer.c) is true for `acwrite` (Vim's is not, so Vim writes `edit foo://bar`).\n\n`:restart` relaunches with the same arguments, so the buffer is opened (loaded) again before the session is sourced on UIEnter; `:file foo://bar` then fails with E95 since a loaded buffer has that name.\n\nEven without the E95, `enew` + `file` only names an empty buffer: `BufReadCmd` is not triggered, so the restored buffer has no content, unlike with `:edit`.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```lua\n-- acw.lua: a minimal \"plugin\" with acwrite buffers\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(\"BufReadCmd\", {\n  pattern = \"foo://*\",\n  callback = function(ev)\n    vim.api.nvim_buf_set_lines(ev.buf, 0, -1, false, { \"content\" })\n  end,\n})\n```\n\n```sh\nnvim --clean -c 'luafile acw.lua' foo://bar -c 'setlocal buftype=acwrite' -c '%argdelete' -c 'mksession! s.vim' -c 'qa!'\nnvim --clean -c 'luafile acw.lua' foo://bar -c 'setlocal buftype=acwrite' -c 'source s.vim'\n```\n\nOr interactively: `nvim --clean -c 'luafile acw.lua' foo://bar`, `:setlocal buftype=acwrite`, then `:restart`.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe session restores the buffer with `:edit foo://bar` (as Vim does), which re-reads it via `BufReadCmd` and does not conflict with an already open buffer.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n`E95: Buffer with this name already exists` at the `file foo://bar` line of the session.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1853+g6edb38ca98\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nmacOS (Darwin 27.2.0)\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\ntmux\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n",
